{"time": "20261117T172213Z", "think": "Hand over the stones.", "command": "say 2", "result": "Never-Writes-Twice: Never-Writes-Twice, at the back of Nesh-Deeka's House. Tells: she looks at each stone and does not take them; the player has done what the order's best could not and is now a Ka-Deelith, a War-Teacher, the fourth rank, with the right to teach the order's fighters; she gives the gauntlets and boots that finish the order's heavier armour. Her watchers have not seen the Unbound anywhere near Teku-Sul, so the player is ahead of them and must go now. The order: dive to Teku-Sul, set the stones in the Kings' Gate, use the Eye where it sits so that strength runs down every root and every tree is healed; do not lift it, for lifted it parts the trees. Then take the stones back from the gate and bring them to her, so the chamber is sealed for good and nobody reaches the Eye again. Then find Cuts-the-Old-Knot and kill her, and rid the marsh of the Unbound. She asks which weapon of the order the player will carry: the pike or the claws (topic.mn17-pike and topic.mn17-claws). Fallback when the stones are not all held: bring all three.\nTopics you can pick:\n1. What do the order's ranks mean?\n2. I have all three seal-stones.\n3. The pike.\n4. The claws.\n5. How do you know the Unbound are not at Teku-Sul?\n6. Fort Chalkmoth\n7. Remind me what we are hunting, and why.", "summary": {"stage": 10, "at": "helstrom", "items": {"item.lockpick": 2, "thing.mn.unbound-note": 1, "item.mn05.voh-vastei-armour": 1, "thing.mn.eye-setting": 1, "thing.mn.keystone": 1, "thing.mn.grave-stake": 1, "thing.mn.paralysis-poison": 3, "thing.mn.bronze-disc": 1, "thing.mn.parchment-map": 1, "thing.mn10.rapier": 1, "thing.mn12.sap-jar": 1, "thing.mn13.reelka-cuirass": 1, "thing.mn13.reelka-helm": 1, "thing.mn.seal-stone-thief": 1, "thing.mn.seal-stone-vault": 1, "thing.mn16.bronze-key": 1, "thing.mn.seal-stone-deep": 1}, "gold": 1650, "flags": {"flag.mn03.truth": true, "flag.mn06.note-read": tr